# TrueCraft+ Real Survival - gameplay guide
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§2========== TrueCraft+ Real Survival =========="}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eTemperature §7- your body runs 0 (freezing) to 100 (heat exhaustion). Biome, night, rain, snow and wet clothes cool you; sun, deserts and metal armor heat you. Campfires and torches warm you up."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eClothing §7- §fleather = warm (mountains, forests), §fchain = breathable (deserts), §firon = conducts heat (colder in snow, hotter in sun), §fgold = absorbs sun, §fdiamond/netherite = strong but heavy."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eThirst §7- §fsneak while standing in water to drink raw (small sickness chance). §fSneak with a water bottle for safe water. §fSneak with a bottle while NEXT TO A CAMPFIRE to boil and drink it - always safe and the best hydration. Eating snow gives a little water but cools you down."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eWeight §7- armor and cargo slow you down and drain stamina. Iron is heavy, leather is light. Travel smart."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eCamping §7- a campfire nearby warms and dries you. Campfire + bed + wood around you = §aSafe Camp§7: slow regeneration and fast temperature recovery."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eExploration §7- discovering new biomes, traveling and finding old camps, small ruins and forgotten storage boxes grants exploration points."}]}
tellraw @s {"rawtext":[{"text":"§eMilestones §7- Day 1 shelter, Day 5 food source, Day 10 equipment, Day 30 permanent home, Day 100 complete survival base."}]}
